        "original_id": "186f897a-4ece-5923-9106-5055d06c5d59",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Araya, Marcus Mumford\n- Bands: Slayer, Mumford & Sons\n- Songs: \"Eyes of the Insane\", \"30/30-150\"\n- Events: 49th Annual Grammy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Tomás Enrique Araya Díaz was born on June 6, 1961, and he is a Chilean American musician.\n- Tom Araya is best known as the vocalist and bassist of the American thrash metal band Slayer.\n- Marcus Oliver Johnstone Mumford was born on 31 January 1987, and he is a British-American singer, songwriter, musician, and producer.\n- Marcus Mumford is best known as the lead singer of the band Mumford & Sons.\n- Tom Araya wrote the song \"Eyes of the Insane\" during pre-production for its album.\n- At the 49th Annual Grammy Awards, the song \"30/30-150\" was nominated for Best Metal Performance but lost to \"Eyes of the Insane\" by Slayer.",
